    "A check-in *each evening.*" to "每天晚上*一次檢視。*",
    "A chronological feed of every migraine, trigger, prodrome, medicine, relief, activity, location and missed activity.\n\nFilter the view by type or time range, or jump straight to \"Needs attention\" to see entries with missing fields (an attack with no end time, a migraine with no severity, a quick-logged item waiting for details).\n\nTap any entry to open it in edit mode and fill in what's missing. The number badge on the tab itself shows how many entries currently need attention so you don't have to remember to come back." to "依時間順序列出每一筆偏頭痛、誘因、前驅症狀、藥物、緩解、活動、地點和錯過的活動。\n\n你可以依類型或時間範圍篩選檢視,也可以直接跳到「需要留意」,查看欄位不完整的紀錄(例如沒有結束時間的發作、沒有嚴重程度的偏頭痛,或等待補充詳細資料的快速記錄)。\n\n點一下任何一筆紀錄即可進入編輯模式,補上缺少的內容。分頁上的數字徽章會顯示目前有多少筆紀錄需要留意,你不用特地記得回來查看。",
    "A clear pull along the side or back of the neck, easing as you hold. Most days for a few weeks is where the benefit comes from. Never stretch into sharp pain." to "頸部側面或後方有明顯的拉伸感,維持姿勢時會逐漸放鬆。連續幾週在大部分日子都做,才能看到效果。千萬不要拉到出現刺痛。",
    "A clear wall, a bed or a mat, a tennis ball" to "一面淨空的牆、床或墊子、網球",
    "A client accepted your appointment time" to "有客戶接受了你的預約時間",
    "A client declined your appointment time" to "有客戶婉拒了你的預約時間",
    "A client suggested an appointment time" to "有客戶建議了預約時間",
    "A day at a desk leaves the chest tight and the shoulders rounded forward. Your head follows them, and once it sits forward of your shoulders it hangs off the muscles at the back of your neck." to "整天坐在桌前,胸口會變緊,肩膀也往前圈。你的頭會跟著前移,一旦頭跑到肩膀前方,就得靠頸部後側的肌肉撐著。",
    "A day without an attack." to "沒有發作的一天。",
    "A few hours" to "幾個小時",
    "A few per year" to "每年幾次",
    "A few questions about your migraines" to "幾個關於你偏頭痛的問題",
    "A first conversation, free and with no obligation. They will see your note and either accept or decline. Nothing is booked, and none of your diary is shared by asking." to "第一次交流,免費、無須承諾。對方會看到你的留言,然後接受或婉拒。不會預約任何服務,提出請求也不會分享你日誌中的任何內容。",
    "A free month on us, and a quick question" to "我們送你一個月免費,再問一個小問題",
    "A full day" to "一整天",
    "A guided entry of the whole attack. Skipping steps is fine, share as much as you care to." to "引導式記錄整次發作。可以跳過步驟,想分享多少都隨你。",
    "A guided evening review of your day in one go. Walks you through a free-text note about how the day went, anything notable from your calendar, and a quick pass over your triggers, prodromes, medicines, reliefs and activities so nothing slips through.\n\nWhen you have an open migraine, it also asks about postdrome symptoms.\n\nIf you're on any treatments, it checks in about side effects from each one.\n\nUse it once a day to keep your log complete without remembering everything at the moment it happens." to "引導式的晚間回顧,一次完成當天的整理。你可以用文字自由記下今天過得如何、查看行事曆中值得注意的事項,再快速檢視你的誘因、前驅症狀、藥物、緩解方式和活動,避免遺漏。\n\n如果你有尚未結束的偏頭痛,也會詢問後期症狀。\n\n如果你正在接受治療,會逐一詢問各項治療的副作用。\n\n每天使用一次,不必在事情發生的當下記住所有細節,也能讓紀錄保持完整。",
    "A little" to "一點點",
    "A metric" to "指標",
    "A more useful read on top of the patterns we've already found in your data. The AI takes what's showing up (the items that turn up around your attacks, the combinations that look risky together, the treatments that seem to be helping) and adds a personal next step for each one, across six categories.\n\nWhat it looks at per category:\n• Triggers: the ones that keep showing up before attacks, and the pairs that look especially risky together. Gives you a preventive action tied to your pattern.\n• Prodromes: your personal early warning signs, with interventions that may abort or shorten an attack when they appear.\n• Medicines: rebound and overuse flags (triptans, NSAIDs, paracetamol, opioids), alternatives when something isn't relieving well, side-effect mitigation, same-class swaps, doctor-discussion prompts. All tied to your own usage.\n• Reliefs: same angles for non-drug methods (alternatives, technique tweaks, timing).\n• Activities: links your timing (exercise, sleep, stress) to context like cortisol and dehydration.\n• Symptoms: the ones running high or severe in your attacks, with targeted prep (anti-emetic on hand, dim-room kit, postdrome plan).\n\nEach recommendation comes with a short evidence line so you can see why it's being suggested. Dismiss anything that doesn't match your reality and it won't come back. These are starting points to discuss with your neurologist, not diagnoses." to "在我們已從你的資料中找到的規律之上,提供更實用的解讀。AI 會根據目前浮現的內容(發作前後經常出現的項目、一起出現時看起來風險較高的組合、似乎有幫助的治療),為每一項加上個人化的下一步建議,涵蓋六個類別。\n\n各類別的分析內容:\n• 誘因:發作前一再出現的誘因,以及同時出現時風險特別高的組合。並提供與你的規律相關的預防做法。\n• 前驅症狀:你個人的早期警訊,以及出現時可能中止或縮短發作的做法。\n• 藥物:反彈與過度使用的警示(曲普坦類、NSAID、乙醯胺酚、鴉片類)、效果不佳時的替代方案、副作用的緩解、同類藥物的替換、與醫師討論的提示。全部依據你自己的使用情況。\n• 緩解方式:針對非藥物方法的相同面向(替代方案、技巧調整、時機)。\n• 活動:將你的時間安排(運動、睡眠、壓力)與皮質醇、脫水等背景因素連結。\n• 症狀:在你的發作中偏高或偏嚴重的症狀,並提供針對性的準備(備好止吐藥、昏暗房間用品、後期症狀計畫)。\n\n每項建議都附有一行簡短的依據,讓你知道為何會提出。不符合你實際情況的建議可以忽略,之後就不會再出現。這些只是可與神經科醫師討論的起點,並非診斷。",
    "A note on Link: linking treatments combines them into one shared % change. " to "關於「連結」的說明:連結治療後,會合併為一個共用的 % 變化。 ",
    "A phrase that names nothing specific is never guessed: it stays in your words unless you pick what it was." to "沒有指明具體內容的用語,絕不會被猜測:除非你選出它指的是什麼,否則會保留你原本的說法。",
    "A push every Monday when your review and new suggestions are ready" to "每週一推播通知,當你的回顧和新建議準備好時",
    "A randomised trial in migraine backs the filter approach. Worth knowing they are much darker than normal tinted glasses." to "一項針對偏頭痛的隨機對照試驗支持濾鏡這種做法。要注意的是,這類鏡片比一般的有色眼鏡暗得多。",
    "A reality check on your risk gauge. We look back at every day you've used the app and ask two questions: when the gauge said HIGH or MILD, did an attack actually happen? And when an attack happened, was the gauge warning the day before?\n\nThat gives you two numbers:\n• Hit rate: of all your attack days, what share the gauge correctly flagged as high-risk beforehand.\n• False alarm rate: of all your non-attack days, what share the gauge flagged anyway.\n\nTap in for the full breakdown (true positives, missed attacks, etc.) and to review any pending recalibration proposals. To tune the LOW / MILD / HIGH thresholds and the day-by-day decay curve yourself, open the menu and tap Risk Model. Lowering the HIGH threshold catches more attacks (higher hit rate) but also more false alarms; raising it does the opposite.\n\nThe weekly recalibration uses these same numbers to nudge your thresholds in the right direction: too many false alarms means thresholds get raised; missed attacks means they get lowered. Changes are incremental (around 20-30% per pass) so the gauge gradually homes in on what works for you.\n\nNeeds at least 7 days of logged data to start showing." to "對你的風險儀表做一次實際驗證。我們會回顧你使用 App 的每一天,並問兩個問題:當儀表顯示「高」或「輕微」時,是否真的發生了發作?而發作發生時,儀表前一天有沒有預警?\n\n由此得出兩個數字:\n• 命中率:在你所有的發作日中,儀表事前正確標示為高風險的比例。\n• 誤報率:在你所有沒有發作的日子中,儀表仍然標示為風險的比例。\n\n點進去可查看完整明細(正確預警、漏掉的發作等),並檢視待處理的重新校正建議。若想自行調整「低 / 輕微 / 高」的門檻和逐日衰減曲線,請開啟選單並點選「風險模型」。調低「高」門檻能抓到更多發作(命中率較高),但誤報也會變多;調高則相反。\n\n每週的重新校正會用同樣的數字,把你的門檻往正確方向微調:誤報太多,門檻就會調高;漏掉發作,就會調低。每次調整幅度不大(每次約 20-30%),讓儀表逐漸貼近適合你的設定。\n\n至少需要 7 天的紀錄資料才會開始顯示。",
    "A reminder from your practitioner" to "來自你的醫療人員的提醒",
    "A scrollable record of every migraine you've logged. Use the arrows on the card to flip through them one at a time, left for older and right for newer. The compact view shows the type, date, duration, severity, and how many of each linked item (triggers, prodromes, medicines, reliefs, locations, activities) you tagged on that attack, with a coloured dot per category.\n\nTap the card to open the full Migraine Timeline screen, where you can:\n• Filter the list by time range (last 7 days, last month, custom range) and by category tags.\n• See each attack as a window of days around it, with every linked event plotted on a timeline so you can see what built up before, during, and lingered after.\n• Switch which migraine sits at the centre of the window using the same arrows.\n\nThis is the place to dig into a specific attack: what was going on the day before, what you took, when you took it, what helped, and what symptoms lingered after." to "可捲動瀏覽的紀錄,收錄你記錄過的每一次偏頭痛。用卡片上的箭頭逐筆翻閱,往左是較舊的,往右是較新的。精簡檢視會顯示類型、日期、持續時間、嚴重程度,以及你在該次發作標記的各類關聯項目(誘因、前驅症狀、藥物、緩解方式、地點、活動)數量,每個類別以一個彩色圓點表示。\n\n點選卡片可開啟完整的偏頭痛時間軸畫面,你可以:\n• 依時間範圍(最近 7 天、最近一個月、自訂範圍)和類別標籤篩選清單。\n• 以發作前後數天的視窗檢視每次發作,所有關聯事件都標在時間軸上,讓你看出發作前累積了什麼、期間發生了什麼、之後又延續了什麼。\n• 使用同樣的箭頭切換位於視窗中央的偏頭痛。\n\n想深入了解某次發作時,就來這裡:前一天發生了什麼、你吃了什麼藥、何時吃的、什麼有幫助,以及之後還殘留哪些症狀。",
    "A secondary \"Last 4 weeks\" number on the detail screen shows whether things are trending up or down recently.\n\n" to "詳細資料畫面上另有「最近 4 週」的數字,顯示近期的趨勢是上升還是下降。\n\n",
    "A simple picture of the activities and locations you've tagged on your migraine logs. For each one we show how often it showed up alongside an attack (count and percentage of your attacks) and the average severity of those attacks compared to your overall average. Higher than usual gets flagged red; lower gets flagged green.\n\nThe preview shows the top 2 by frequency. Tap in for the full list.\n\nImportant: this only counts activities and locations you've actually linked to a specific migraine (via the Activities and Locations steps in the full wizard, or in the Daily Check-In). It's not a correlation analysis like What Happened; it's a straight tally of what was around when you logged each attack. If you don't tag activities or locations, nothing shows up here." to "簡單呈現你在偏頭痛紀錄中標記的活動和地點。每一項都會顯示它與發作同時出現的頻率(次數及占你發作的百分比),以及這些發作的平均嚴重程度與你整體平均的比較。高於平常會標示為紅色,低於平常則標示為綠色。\n\n預覽會顯示出現頻率最高的前 2 項。點進去可查看完整清單。\n\n重要:這裡只計算你實際連結到特定偏頭痛的活動和地點(透過完整精靈中的「活動」和「地點」步驟,或每日檢視)。這不是像「發生了什麼」那樣的關聯分析,只是單純統計你記錄每次發作時身邊有什麼。如果你沒有標記活動或地點,這裡就不會顯示任何內容。",
    "A spike in stress" to "壓力驟增",
    "A straight before-and-after of what you've been logging: for every trigger, prodrome, medicine and relief, how often it appeared on the attacks of the last 30 days compared with the 30 days before that.\n\nThis is a tally, not a correlation analysis. It only counts items linked to an attack, and it only compares the two date windows — nothing is filtered or weighted. An item shows up here the moment its count moved between the two periods.\n\nColours give you the read at a glance: an unwanted item (trigger, prodrome, medicine) climbing shows red, easing off shows green. Reliefs work the other way round: using them more shows green.\n\nIf your acute medication count is climbing fast, a small note flags it. Medication-overuse headache is a real thing, and catching the trend early is exactly what this card is for.\n\nThe preview shows the two biggest movers. Tap in for the full list, matching the What changed page of the PDF report." to "直接呈現前後對比:針對你記錄的每個誘因、前驅症狀、藥物和緩解方式,比較最近 30 天的發作與更早之前 30 天的發作中出現的頻率。\n\n這只是統計,不是關聯分析。只計算與發作相關聯的項目,也只比較這兩個日期區間,不做任何篩選或加權。只要某項目的次數在兩個期間之間有變動,就會顯示在這裡。\n\n顏色讓你一眼看懂:不想要的項目(誘因、前驅症狀、藥物)增加時顯示紅色,減少時顯示綠色。緩解方式則相反:用得更多會顯示綠色。\n\n如果你的急性用藥次數快速上升,會出現一則小提醒。藥物過度使用性頭痛確實存在,及早發現趨勢正是這張卡片的用途。\n\n預覽會顯示變動最大的兩項。點進去可查看完整清單,內容與 PDF 報告的「變化」頁相同。",
