    "How you train" to "訓練方式",
    "How your attacks went when you used each medicine and relief" to "使用各種藥物和緩解方式時,你的發作情況如何",
    "How your attacks went when you used each medicine and relief. This is your own log read back to you, not a measure of the drug.\n\nEvery treatment you logged gets a row, and every row gets one of the same four verdicts, so you can compare them at a glance:\n• Works well — measured improvement, or you rated it high relief.\n• Some help — a smaller effect, or a mild rating.\n• No clear effect — measured and found nothing, or you rated it low or none.\n• Not enough yet — logged, but nothing to judge on.\n\nUnderneath, one line says where the verdict came from, in the unit it was measured in:\n• Pain points, when you log pain during an attack. We compare the three hours before a dose with the reading around two hours after, inside the same attack.\n• Pain points against your untreated attacks, when you don't. This one is deliberately cautious: you reach for treatment on your worse attacks, so it understates the benefit. That's why it reads \"at least\".\n• Hours, when we have enough ended-at times to compare an attack's length against your untreated attacks of the same severity.\n• Your own relief rating, in the words you picked, when there isn't enough to measure.\n\nWhere we have dose times, a second line splits your uses at your own median delay for that treatment and shows the peak pain either side. It is your habit, not a clinical window.\n\nThe dots show how much is behind the finding. One dot is a weak result honestly shown, not an error.\n\nFindings sharpen with more logging, especially relief ratings, dose times and ended-at times on each attack. \"Took something but didn't note what\" can't feed into this." to "你使用各種藥物與緩解方式時,發作的情況如何。這是把你自己的記錄回饋給你,並不是對藥物本身的評估。\n\n你記錄過的每種治療都會有一列,每一列都會得到相同四種判定之一,方便你一眼比較:\n• 效果良好:有測量到的改善,或你評為高度緩解。\n• 有些幫助:效果較小,或你給了輕微的評分。\n• 沒有明顯效果:已測量但沒有發現效果,或你評為低度緩解或沒有緩解。\n• 資料還不夠:已記錄,但還沒有足夠的資料可以判斷。\n\n下方有一行說明判定的依據,並以測量時使用的單位表示:\n• 疼痛分數:當你在發作期間記錄疼痛時使用。我們會在同一次發作中,比較服藥前三小時與服藥後約兩小時的數值。\n• 與未治療發作相比的疼痛分數:當你沒有記錄發作期間的疼痛時使用。這項做法刻意採取保守估計:你通常在較嚴重的發作時才會用藥,所以會低估治療的益處。因此這裡會顯示「至少」。\n• 小時:當我們有足夠的結束時間,可以將一次發作的時間長度與你嚴重程度相同的未治療發作比較時使用。\n• 你自己的緩解評分,以你選擇的用語呈現:當資料不足以進行測量時使用。\n\n若有服藥時間,第二行會以你對該治療的服藥延遲中位數,將你的使用分成兩組,並顯示兩邊的疼痛高峰。這反映的是你的習慣,不是臨床建議的時間範圍。\n\n圓點代表這項結果背後有多少資料支持。一個圓點代表結果薄弱,但如實呈現,並不是錯誤。\n\n記錄得越多,結果就越準確,尤其是緩解評分、服藥時間,以及每次發作的結束時間。「吃了藥但沒有記下是什麼」這種情況無法納入分析。",
    "How your attacks went when you used each one. From your own log, not a measure of the medicine." to "使用各項時你的發作情況如何。資料來自你自己的記錄,並非對藥物效果的衡量。",
