    "Symptoms you flag as caused by your treatments" to "你標示為治療所引起的症狀",
    "Symptoms you flag as caused by your treatments, medicines or reliefs" to "你標示為由治療、藥物或緩解方式引起的症狀",
    "Symptoms, Medicines & More" to "症狀、藥物與更多",
    "Syncing Health Data" to "正在同步健康資料",
    "Syncing health data from Health Connect" to "正在從 Health Connect 同步健康資料",
    "T0" to "T0",
    "THE ATTACK" to "這次發作",
    "THE TOUR" to "導覽",
    "TIMELINE" to "時間軸",
    "TV / film" to "電視 / 電影",
    "Take 15 seconds to log your day" to "花 15 秒記錄你的一天",
    "Take any medicine?" to "有服用藥物嗎?",
    "Take the Full Tour" to "完整導覽",
    "Take the Tour" to "開始導覽",
    "Take the full tour" to "開始完整導覽",
    "Take the tour" to "開始導覽",
    "Takeaways, instant noodles, stock cubes" to "外帶餐點、泡麵、高湯塊",
    "Taken within %1\$s (your median delay): peak %2\$s · later: peak %3\$s" to "%1\$s 內服用(你的延遲中位數):高峰 %2\$s · 較晚服用:高峰 %3\$s",
    "Takes about 5 minutes. You can leave the tour at any point." to "大約需要 5 分鐘。你可以隨時離開導覽。",
    "Taking longer than expected..." to "花的時間比預期久...",
    "Talk through your day — voice-powered evening check-ins." to "說說你的一天——用語音完成晚間記錄。",
    "Talk, type, or import a file from another app. We fill in what you tell us, then suggest what else is worth tracking. You can change it all on the next pages." to "可以用說的、打字,或從其他 App 匯入檔案。我們會填入你告訴我們的內容,再建議還有哪些值得追蹤。你可以在後面幾頁修改所有內容。",
    "Tap + to start the conversation!" to "點選 + 開始對話!",
    "Tap Add Treatment to start tracking a drug, device, or lifestyle change." to "點選「新增治療」,開始追蹤藥物、裝置或生活習慣的改變。",
    "Tap Connect on the Health Connect card above." to "點選上方 Health Connect 卡片的「連接」。",
    "Tap Connect on your wearable below." to "請在下方點一下你的穿戴裝置的「連接」。",
    "Tap Connect on yours below." to "在下方你的那一項點選「連接」。",
    "Tap Full Report for the PDF, or AI Recommendations to review and accept or reject each suggestion with one tap." to "點一下「完整報告」可取得 PDF,或點一下「AI 建議」,只需輕點一下就能檢視並接受或拒絕每則建議。",
    "Tap Log Migraine for the full 13-step wizard (timing, symptoms, pain, prodromes, triggers, medicines, reliefs, locations, activities, postdromes, missed activities, notes, review).\n\nIf you're in the middle of an attack, there's an \"It's happening right now\" shortcut on the timing step that saves the entry in one tap so you don't have to answer 12 more questions while in pain.\n\nBelow the hero card is Quick Log: one-tap entry for a single migraine, prodrome, trigger, medicine, relief, or symptom without a full wizard.\n\nPick Aura as a symptom anywhere and a short sheet opens so you can mark where in your vision it appeared and how long it lasted. You can skip it, and you can change it later by tapping Aura again.\n\nDaily Check-In is the evening rollup where the app lists everything it caught automatically (sleep, weather, nutrition, activity) and you confirm, plus capture postdrome symptoms tied to today's attack." to "點選「記錄偏頭痛」即可進入完整的 13 步引導流程（時間、症狀、疼痛、前驅症狀、誘因、藥物、緩解方式、地點、活動、後期症狀、錯過的活動、備註、確認）。\n\n如果你正處於發作中，時間這一步有「正在發生」的捷徑，只要點一下就能儲存記錄，不必在疼痛時再回答另外 12 個問題。\n\n主卡片下方是快速記錄：不需要完整流程，點一下就能記錄單一的偏頭痛、前驅症狀、誘因、藥物、緩解方式或症狀。\n\n在任何地方選擇預兆作為症狀時，都會跳出一個簡短的頁面，讓你標示預兆出現在視野的哪個位置、持續多久。你可以略過，之後也可以再點一次預兆來修改。\n\n每日檢視是晚間的彙整：App 會列出自動擷取到的所有內容（睡眠、天氣、營養、活動）讓你確認，也可以補記與今天發作相關的後期症狀。",
    "Tap Log Migraine, or just talk. Triggers your watch and phone caught are already ticked, with the time they hit." to "點選「記錄偏頭痛」，或直接開口說。手錶和手機偵測到的誘因已先勾選好，並附上發生的時間。",
    "Tap a bar to edit · Risk points per day relative to predicted ovulation" to "點選長條可編輯 · 相對預測排卵日的每日風險點數",
    "Tap a bar to edit · Risk points per day relative to predicted period" to "點選長條可編輯 · 相對預測經期的每日風險點數",
    "Tap a favourite to log it now" to "點選常用項目即可立即記錄",
    "Tap a × to remove an item, type to add one." to "點選 × 移除項目,輸入文字即可新增。",
    "Tap all that apply" to "點選所有符合的項目",
    "Tap any chip below to limit the report to attacks matching it." to "點選下方任一標籤,報告就只顯示符合的發作。",
    "Tap any chip below to narrow the report down to just the migraine attacks that have that severity / symptom / trigger / medicine / etc. Multiple chips stack — picking a Trigger plus a Symptom shows only attacks with both. Chips are grouped by category and only the values that appear in your logs show up here." to "點選下方任一標籤，就能將報告縮小到只顯示具有該嚴重程度／症狀／誘因／藥物等的偏頭痛發作。可同時選擇多個標籤，例如選了一個誘因加一個症狀，就只會顯示兩者兼具的發作。標籤依類別分組，且只會顯示出現在你記錄中的項目。",
    "Tap any day on the 7-day forecast strip to preview future risk, or tap the gauge for the full contributor breakdown." to "點一下 7 天預測列中的任何一天,即可預覽未來的風險;或點一下儀表,查看完整的影響因素明細。",
    "Tap any entry to edit it. Use the \"Needs attention\" filter when the tab shows a number so you can clean those up in one pass." to "點一下任何紀錄即可編輯。當分頁顯示數字時,可使用「需要留意」篩選,一次整理完這些紀錄。",
    "Tap any icon to log something in one tap with the timestamp set to right now. Use it mid-attack or whenever you don't have the bandwidth for a full log.\n\nIf you've starred favourites in your pools (your usual triggers, rescue medicines, etc.), the button opens a quick sheet of those so you can pick the specific one and confirm. No favourites set, or no time to choose? Tap \"Skip, just log Migraine\" (or \"Trigger\" / \"Medicine\" / etc.) and it saves immediately with a generic label.\n\nYou'll notice postdrome isn't here. That's on purpose: postdromes are the recovery symptoms that belong to a specific migraine, so we want them linked to an attack rather than floating on their own. We'll prompt you for them in your daily check-in whenever you have an open migraine, and you can also log them via the full wizard or by editing the migraine afterwards.\n\nFor a full attack log with timing, symptoms, pain location, prodromes and medicines, use the Log tab. Quick log is the shortcut for when you can't deal with all of that." to "點選任一圖示，就能一鍵記錄，時間會自動設為現在。在發作期間，或沒有餘力完整記錄時都很適用。\n\n如果你已在清單中將常用項目加上星號（例如你常見的誘因、急救藥物等），按鈕會開啟一個快速選單，讓你挑選特定項目並確認。沒有設定最愛，或沒時間選擇？點選「略過，直接記錄偏頭痛」（或「誘因」／「藥物」等），就會立即以通用名稱儲存。\n\n你會發現這裡沒有後期症狀，這是刻意的：後期症狀是特定一次偏頭痛的恢復期症狀，所以我們希望它們連結到某次發作，而不是單獨存在。只要你有尚未結束的偏頭痛，我們就會在每日檢視中詢問你；你也可以透過完整的記錄精靈，或事後編輯該次偏頭痛來記錄。\n\n如果要完整記錄一次發作，包括時間、症狀、疼痛位置、前驅症狀和藥物，請使用「記錄」分頁。快速記錄則是在你無法處理這一切時的捷徑。",
    "Tap any metric to add it to the graph. Highlighted ones have been detected in your migraine data." to "點選任一指標即可加入圖表。醒目標示的是在你的偏頭痛資料中偵測到的指標。",
    "Tap any provider card to connect or disconnect. Connecting opens the provider's own login screen; disconnecting stops the data pull but keeps everything you've already imported." to "點選任一服務供應商卡片即可連接或中斷連線。連接會開啟該供應商自己的登入畫面;中斷連線會停止擷取資料,但會保留你已匯入的所有內容。",
    "Tap any signs you notice before a migraine — we've pre-selected what we found" to "點選你在偏頭痛前注意到的徵兆——我們已先選好找到的項目",
    "Tap any threshold circle to edit it, or use the per-day decay curve below. Changes save instantly." to "點一下任何門檻圓圈即可編輯,或使用下方的每日衰減曲線。變更會立即儲存。",
    "Tap any value below to adjust it. You can always fine-tune these later in Settings → Risk Model." to "點選下方任一數值即可調整。之後也可隨時在「設定 → 風險模型」中微調。",
    "Tap anything that happened" to "點選發生過的事項",
    "Tap anything that helps — dark room, cold compress, sleep, caffeine." to "點選有幫助的項目——暗室、冷敷、睡眠、咖啡因。",
    "Tap anything that lingers once the migraine is over — fatigue, brain fog, mood crash" to "點選偏頭痛結束後仍持續的狀況——疲倦、腦霧、情緒低落",
    "Tap anything that triggers your migraines — we've pre-selected what we found" to "點選會引發你偏頭痛的誘因——我們已先選好找到的項目",
    "Tap anything you did" to "點選你做過的事",
    "Tap anything you regularly miss because of migraines." to "點選你常因偏頭痛而錯過的事項。",
    "Tap anything you skipped or cancelled" to "點選你略過或取消的事",
    "Tap for full timeline with graph & filters" to "點選查看完整時間軸、圖表與篩選",
    "Tap into the detail screen and you'll get:\n" to "進入詳細頁面,你會看到:\n",
    "Tap one to see everything we read from it." to "點選其中一項,查看我們讀取的所有內容。",
    "Tap places where you usually get migraines — patterns here can point to specific triggers" to "點選你常發生偏頭痛的地點——這裡的規律可能指向特定誘因",
    "Tap regenerate to build your summary." to "點選重新產生,建立你的摘要。",
    "Tap the dots on the head to mark where it hurts" to "點選頭部的圓點,標示疼痛的位置",
    "Tap the heart on any article to save it" to "點選文章上的愛心即可收藏",
    "Tap the mic and talk, or type below. We'll fill in what you tell us directly, then suggest what else is worth tracking based on your profile — you can adjust it all on the next pages." to "點一下麥克風開始說話,或在下方輸入。我們會直接填入你告訴我們的內容,再根據你的個人資料建議其他值得追蹤的項目,你可以在接下來的頁面調整這一切。",
    "Tap the migraine type you usually get under Pain Character, plus anything that tags along under Accompanying." to "在「疼痛特性」下點選你常見的偏頭痛類型，並在「伴隨症狀」下點選隨之出現的狀況。",
    "Tap the slider to pick what you want to see." to "點選滑桿,選擇你想查看的內容。",
    "Tap to add how it ended." to "點選以補充結束情況。",
    "Tap to add how it ended. We won't ask about this one again." to "點選以補充結束情況。我們不會再詢問這一筆。",
    "Tap to edit" to "點一下編輯",
    "Tap to log an attack starting now. Add details later." to "點選即可記錄現在開始的發作。細節稍後再補。",
    "Tap to open the detail screen with: Customize Medicines (pick favourites and " to "點選開啟詳細頁面:自訂藥物(選出常用項目並",
    "Tap to set up cycle tracking" to "點選以設定週期追蹤",
    "Tap to speak" to "點一下說話",
    "Tap to start" to "點選開始",
    "Tap to toggle metric lines. Highlighted chips were logged with this attack." to "點選以切換指標線。醒目標示的項目已與這次發作一併記錄。",
    "Tap to toggle. ⚡ = auto-detected." to "點選切換。⚡ = 自動偵測。",
    "Tap what applies. Add details or skip." to "點選符合的項目。可補充細節或略過。",
    "Tap what you're usually doing when a migraine hits." to "點選偏頭痛發作時你通常正在做的事。",
    "Tap what's appeared since you logged it" to "點選記錄後新出現的項目",
    "Tap your avatar to update your photo. Rerun onboarding from this screen if you want to walk through the tour again later." to "點一下你的大頭貼即可更新照片。之後如果想再看一次導覽,可以在此畫面重新執行新手引導。",
    "Tearing" to "流淚",
    "Teeth Left" to "左側牙齒",
    "Teeth Right" to "右側牙齒",
    "Tell us about a trigger you didn't expect — the one that took you ages to figure out." to "告訴我們一個你意想不到的誘因——那個讓你花了很久才找出來的。",
    "Tell us about your day" to "說說你今天的情況",
    "Tell us about your migraines" to "說說你的偏頭痛",
    "Tell us about your migraines…" to "跟我們說說你的偏頭痛…",
    "Tell us about yourself and answer some questions." to "跟我們介紹一下你自己,並回答幾個問題。",
    "Temp" to "溫度",
    "Temp %s" to "溫度 %s",
    "Temperature" to "溫度",
    "Temperature high" to "溫度偏高",
    "Temperature low" to "溫度偏低",
    "Temple massage" to "太陽穴按摩",
    "Ten real screens, each explained in one card" to "十個真實畫面,每個都用一張卡片說明",
    "Tension" to "緊繃",
    "Tension headache" to "緊張型頭痛",
    "Tension type" to "緊縮型",
    "Terms of Service" to "服務條款",
    "Terms of Use" to "使用條款",
    "Test the \"It's happening right now\" button on the first wizard step; it logs immediately so you can come back and fill in details later." to "在精靈的第一步測試「現在正在發生」按鈕;它會立即記錄,之後你可以再回來補充細節。",
    "Thanks for letting us know. We'll review this content shortly." to "謝謝你告訴我們,我們會儘快審查這則內容。",
    "That Cliniko key is not allowed to book appointments." to "這組 Cliniko 金鑰沒有預約權限。",
    "That account is not set up as a practitioner." to "這個帳號尚未設定為執業者。",
    "That client is not connected to you." to "這位客戶尚未與你連結。",
    "That didn't work" to "操作失敗了",
    "That does not look like a web address. Start it with https://" to "這看起來不像網址。請以 https:// 開頭。",
    "That file could not be read as text. Export as CSV, and keep it under 6 MB." to "無法將該檔案讀取為文字。請匯出為 CSV,並將大小控制在 6 MB 以內。",
    "That is no longer open." to "這項已不再開放。",
    "That range is too long." to "這個範圍太長了。",
    "That request is no longer open." to "這個請求已不再開放。",
    "That request was not found." to "找不到這個請求。",
    "That suggestion is no longer open." to "這個建議已不再開放。",
    "That time has already passed." to "這個時間已經過了。",
    "The AI drafts your triggers, thresholds and pool" to "AI 會草擬你的誘因、門檻值和項目池",
    "The AI learns from what you log either way. Answering the setup questions gives it your own account of your migraines to start from — sleep, stress, food, weather, hormones and warning signs — so its first read of you is closer than a blank page." to "無論如何，AI 都會從你的記錄中學習。回答設定問題，能讓它以你自己對偏頭痛的描述作為起點——睡眠、壓力、飲食、天氣、荷爾蒙和預警徵兆——所以它對你的初步判讀會比從空白開始更貼近你。",
    "The AI needs about five logged attacks before it has anything to say." to "AI 需要大約五次已記錄的發作,才能提供分析。",
    "The AI proposes your profile every Monday, after about 5 attacks" to "AI 每週一提出你的個人檔案,約需 5 次發作",
    "The AI reads what you log and proposes your profile every Monday." to "AI 會讀取你的記錄,並在每週一提出你的個人檔案。",
    "The actual app behaviour is driven by what you currently have in Manage Items and Risk Model, which you can edit any time from the drawer. The weekly AI Calibration card in Insights nudges those values over time as the app learns from your data." to "App 實際的運作方式取決於你目前在「管理項目」和「風險模型」中的內容,你隨時可以從側邊選單編輯。「洞察」中每週的 AI 校準卡片,會隨著 App 從你的資料中學習,逐步調整這些數值。",
    "The app is ready for the tour." to "App 已準備好導覽。",
    "The app only records noise levels (decibels), not conversations or identifiable audio." to "App 只會記錄噪音程度(分貝),不會錄下對話或可辨識的聲音。",
    "The best studied device on this list. Randomised trials support both stopping an attack and reducing how often they come." to "這是清單中研究最充分的裝置。隨機試驗支持它既能中止發作,也能降低發作頻率。",
    "The big one. A single scrollable report that pulls every angle we have on your data into one place: frequency over time, top patterns and trigger interactions, which treatments and lifestyle changes are working, the activities and locations that surround your attacks, severity, pain location and aura breakdowns, missed-activity counts, plus the full migraine timeline with spider charts of what was happening around each attack.\n\nThe raw inputs are tweakable. You can edit any logged migraine, change a trigger or prodrome's severity in Manage Items, and filter the whole report by time range or tags. The AI-derived parts (Recommendations and the What Happened pattern findings) aren't directly editable; they recompute live from whatever data you've kept in.\n\nUseful for sharing with your neurologist or just getting a quarterly read of how things are trending. Everything you see in the individual cards below is in here too, but stitched together so patterns across categories become obvious." to "重頭戲。這是一份可連續捲動的完整報告，把我們掌握的你的資料各個面向集中在同一處：隨時間變化的頻率、主要規律和誘因之間的交互作用、哪些治療和生活方式調整有效、發作前後的活動和地點、嚴重程度、疼痛位置和預兆的分析、錯過活動的次數，以及完整的偏頭痛時間軸，並附上每次發作前後情況的雷達圖。\n\n原始輸入的資料都可以調整。你可以編輯任何已記錄的偏頭痛，在「管理項目」中更改誘因或前驅症狀的嚴重程度，也可以依時間範圍或標籤篩選整份報告。由 AI 產生的部分（建議，以及「發生了什麼」中的規律發現）無法直接編輯；它們會根據你保留的資料即時重新計算。\n\n很適合與你的神經科醫師分享，或只是每季看看整體趨勢。下方各張卡片中的所有內容也都在這裡，只是整合在一起，讓跨類別的規律更容易看出來。",
    "The chat assistant is available for premium subscribers. Upgrade to get personalised health insights from your data." to "聊天助理僅限 Premium 訂閱者使用。升級後即可根據你的資料取得個人化的健康洞察。",
    "The daily risk score the app showed you" to "App 顯示給你的每日風險分數",
    "The downstream story: not what caused your attacks, but what they looked like and what you missed because of them.\n• Severity distribution: how your attacks break down across the 1-10 scale. Useful for spotting whether you mostly get moderate ones or whether you're getting a creeping number of severe ones.\n• Pain locations: which sides and zones of your head get hit most. Pulled from the Pain step in the wizard.\n• Aura location: if you log an aura, where in your field of vision it appears and how long it lasts, drawn as you see it through your own eyes. Only shows once you've logged at least one aura.\n• Top symptoms: which symptoms show up most often, with the average severity and duration of the attacks they appear in. Comes from your linked symptom logs.\n• Missed activities: the things you've explicitly tagged as missed because of an attack, ranked by how often they came up.\n\nTap in for the full breakdown.\n\nLike the other cards, this only counts data you've logged. If you don't rate severity, pick pain locations, or tag missed activities in your wizard, those sections stay empty." to "後續的故事：不是什麼引起了你的發作，而是發作時的樣子，以及你因此錯過了什麼。\n• 嚴重程度分布：你的發作在 1–10 分量表上的分布情形。有助於看出你多半是中度發作，還是重度發作正在悄悄增加。\n• 疼痛位置：你頭部哪些側邊和區域最常疼痛。資料來自精靈中的「疼痛」步驟。\n• 預兆位置：如果你有記錄預兆，會顯示它出現在視野的哪個位置以及持續多久，並以你親眼所見的方式繪製。至少記錄過一次預兆後才會顯示。\n• 主要症狀：最常出現的症狀，以及這些症狀所出現發作的平均嚴重程度和持續時間。資料來自你已連結的症狀記錄。\n• 錯過的活動：你明確標記為因發作而錯過的事項，依出現次數排序。\n\n點進去可查看完整分析。\n\n和其他卡片一樣，這裡只會計入你記錄過的資料。如果你沒有評定嚴重程度、選擇疼痛位置，或在精靈中標記錯過的活動，這些區塊就會維持空白。",
    "The factors that showed up before attacks, ranked by strength" to "發作前出現的因素,依影響強度排序",
    "The first few times feel like a lot of effort for nothing. The benefit comes from doing it most days for a few weeks, ideally at the same time, so the body learns the release." to "前幾次可能會讓你覺得花了很多力氣卻沒有效果。好處來自連續幾週、大多數日子都做,最好在同一個時間,讓身體學會放鬆。",
    "The four bands (Not noticeable · Some effect · Showing progress · Working well) follow the clinical responder definition: " to "這四個等級(不明顯 · 有些效果 · 正在進步 · 效果良好)依照臨床上對治療反應者的定義:",
    "The full attack log. Tap to walk through every step that goes into recording a migraine: timing, paint-the-picture AI shortcut, symptoms, pain, prodromes, triggers, medicines, reliefs, locations, activities, postdromes, missed activities, notes, and a final review.\n\nUse this when you want the complete record of an attack and have a few minutes to fill it in. Every step is optional, so skip what doesn't apply.\n\nFor one-tap or single-item logging during an attack, use the Quick Log strip on the Home tab or the Quick Log section below." to "完整的發作記錄。點選後會依序走過記錄一次偏頭痛的每個步驟：時間、用 AI 描述畫面的捷徑、症狀、疼痛、前驅症狀、誘因、藥物、緩解方式、地點、活動、後期症狀、錯過的活動、備註，以及最後的檢視。\n\n當你想完整記錄一次發作，而且有幾分鐘可以填寫時，就用這個。每個步驟都是選填，不適用的可以直接跳過。\n\n如果要在發作期間一鍵記錄或只記錄單一項目，請使用首頁的快速記錄列，或下方的快速記錄區。",
    "The gauge shows how full your bucket is: {Low}, {Mild} or {High}. Under it: the 7 day outlook." to "儀表會顯示你的水桶有多滿:{Low}、{Mild} 或 {High}。下方是未來 7 天的預測。",
    "The hand on the belly is there so you can feel that the breath is going low and slow, not high into the chest." to "把手放在肚子上,是為了讓你感覺到呼吸是又深又慢,而不是淺淺地停在胸口。",
    "The head diagram, and how the pain moved." to "頭部圖示，以及疼痛如何移動。",
    "The more data MigraineMe has, the better it predicts." to "MigraineMe 的資料越多,預測就越準確。",
    "The muscles at the top of your neck and the nerves that carry migraine pain meet in the same part of the brainstem. When those muscles are tight and sore, the brain can read it as head pain, and a neck that is already irritated makes an attack easier to set off." to "頸部上方的肌肉，與傳遞偏頭痛疼痛的神經，會在腦幹的同一個部位交會。當這些肌肉緊繃痠痛時，大腦可能會把它解讀為頭痛，而已經受到刺激的頸部也會讓發作更容易被引發。",
    "The nose slides straight back, like making a double chin, then forward again. Eyes level. Hold a moment, release." to "鼻子沿水平方向直直往後收，就像做出雙下巴，再回到前方。雙眼保持平視。停留片刻後放鬆。",
    "The oldest idea on this page, done with a machine." to "本頁最古老的點子,現在交給機器來做。",
    "The patterns we've found in your data, stacked in three layers:\n• Single factors: the triggers, prodromes, and daily metrics (sleep, weather, HRV, etc.) that show up most around your attacks.\n• Combinations: pairs of factors that look risky together even if each one isn't a big deal alone. The classic example is under-6h sleep on its own being fine, but under-6h sleep paired with a stressful day stacking into a high-risk window.\n• Symptom outcomes: given the trigger you just hit, which symptoms tend to show up.\n\nYou'll see one of two numbers on each finding:\n• \"X× more likely\" — how much more often it happens on the days around your attacks compared with your normal days. We can only show this for things we can fairly compare day to day: signals tracked constantly (sleep, weather, HRV) and manual triggers you log very consistently. This is the stronger read — it means the factor genuinely makes an attack more likely.\n• \"% of your attacks\" — for things you only flag manually and not regularly, where there's no fair day-to-day comparison. It simply shows how often the factor turned up in your attacks. It tells you what your attacks have in common, not that the factor raises your risk.\n\nThe dots show how sure we are: more data behind a finding, more dots. Findings sharpen as you log more — sparse logging means weaker findings, consistent logging means cleaner patterns.\n\nThe preview here shows the top 2 from each layer. Tap in for the full ranked list." to "我們在你的資料中找到的規律,分成三個層次:\n• 單一因素:最常出現在你發作前後的誘因、前驅症狀,以及每日指標(睡眠、天氣、HRV 等)。\n• 組合:兩個因素單獨看影響不大,但湊在一起就有風險。典型的例子是,睡眠不足 6 小時單獨出現沒什麼問題,但睡眠不足 6 小時再加上壓力大的一天,就會疊加成高風險的時段。\n• 症狀結果:在你剛遇到某個誘因時,通常會出現哪些症狀。\n\n每個發現旁會顯示以下兩種數字之一:\n• 「可能性高出 X 倍」——相較於平常的日子,這個因素在你發作前後幾天出現的頻率高出多少。只有能公平逐日比較的項目才會顯示這個數字:持續追蹤的訊號(睡眠、天氣、HRV),以及你記錄得非常規律的手動誘因。這是比較有力的判讀,代表這個因素確實會讓發作更容易發生。\n• 「占你發作的 %」——適用於只靠手動標記、而且不是每天都記錄的項目,因為這類項目無法做公平的逐日比較。它只顯示這個因素出現在你發作中的頻率,說明的是你的發作有哪些共同點,並不代表這個因素會提高你的風險。\n\n圓點代表我們有多少把握:發現背後的資料越多,圓點就越多。你記錄得越多,發現就越準確——記錄零散,發現就比較不可靠;記錄規律,規律就會更清楚。\n\n這裡的預覽會顯示每個層次的前 2 項。點進去可以看完整的排名清單。",
    "The patterns we've found in your data, stacked in three layers:\n• Single factors: the triggers, prodromes, and daily metrics (sleep, weather, HRV, etc.) that show up most around your attacks.\n• Combinations: pairs of factors that look risky together even if each one isn't a big deal alone. The classic example is under-6h sleep on its own being fine, but under-6h sleep paired with a stressful day stacking into a high-risk window.\n• Symptom outcomes: given the trigger you just hit, which symptoms tend to show up.\n\nYou'll see one of two numbers on each finding:\n• \"about 2 times as likely\" — how much more often it happens on the days around your attacks compared with your normal days. We can only show this for things we can fairly compare day to day: signals tracked constantly (sleep, weather, HRV) and manual triggers you log very consistently. This is the stronger read — it means the factor genuinely makes an attack more likely.\n• \"% of your attacks\" — for things you only flag manually and not regularly, where there's no fair day-to-day comparison. It simply shows how often the factor turned up in your attacks. It tells you what your attacks have in common, not that the factor raises your risk.\n\nWhen a finding says \"flare days\", a long attack was counted day by day, so the numbers are attack days rather than attacks.\n\nThe dots show how sure we are: more data behind a finding, more dots. Findings sharpen as you log more — sparse logging means weaker findings, consistent logging means cleaner patterns.\n\nThe preview here shows the top 2 from each layer. Tap in for the full ranked list." to "我們在你的資料中找到的規律，分成三層：\n• 單一因素：在你發作前後最常出現的誘因、前驅症狀和每日指標（睡眠、天氣、HRV 等）。\n• 組合：單獨看影響不大，但同時出現就顯得危險的因素組合。經典例子是：只睡不到 6 小時本身沒問題，但睡不到 6 小時再加上壓力大的一天，就會疊成高風險時段。\n• 症狀結果：碰到剛才那個誘因後，通常會出現哪些症狀。\n\n每項發現會顯示以下兩種數字之一：\n• 「約 2 倍的可能性」— 相較於平常的日子，這個因素在你發作前後幾天出現的頻率高出多少。只有能逐日公平比較的項目才會顯示，例如持續追蹤的訊號（睡眠、天氣、HRV）和你非常規律記錄的手動誘因。這是較有力的判讀，代表該因素確實會提高發作的可能性。\n• 「% 的發作」— 用於只靠手動標記、且不是經常記錄的項目，因為無法做公平的逐日比較。它只顯示該因素在你的發作中出現的頻率，說明的是你的發作有哪些共通點，不代表這個因素會提高你的風險。\n\n當發現中出現「發作日」時，代表一次較長的發作是逐日計算的，所以數字是發作天數，而不是發作次數。\n\n圓點代表我們的把握程度：發現背後的資料越多，圓點越多。你記錄得越多，發現就越精準——記錄稀少，發現較弱；記錄規律，規律更清晰。\n\n這裡的預覽只顯示每一層的前 2 項。點進去可查看完整排名。",
    "The positive side of your data: what you're doing right, tied to your migraine-free days." to "你資料中正面的一面：你做對了什麼，以及它們與你沒有偏頭痛的日子之間的關聯。",
    "The positive side of your data: what you're doing right, tied to your migraine-free days.\n• Well done: habits and steady health signals (consistent sleep, calm stress, steady caffeine, trigger-free eating days) that show up on the days you stay migraine-free. Consistency is the point, staying near your own normal, not hitting anyone else's targets.\n• What drives it: the things that make those habits happen, an active day leading to steadier recovery, alcohol-free days leading to steadier sleep, yoga leading to calmer stress.\n\nEverything here is measured against your own data. Nothing in this card warns or judges; it only shows what is already working so you can keep doing it.\n\nFindings sharpen with more logging. If the card is quiet, it just needs more days of data, not different behaviour." to "你資料中正面的一面：你做對了什麼，與你沒有偏頭痛的日子之間的關聯。\n• 做得好：在你沒有偏頭痛的日子裡出現的習慣和穩定的健康訊號（規律的睡眠、平穩的壓力、穩定的咖啡因攝取、沒有誘因的飲食日）。重點在於穩定，也就是維持在你自己的常態附近，而不是達到別人的目標。\n• 背後的推動因素：讓這些習慣得以實現的事情，例如活躍的一天帶來更穩定的恢復、不喝酒的日子帶來更穩定的睡眠、瑜伽帶來更平穩的壓力。\n\n這裡的一切都是以你自己的資料為基準來衡量。這張卡片不會警告或評判你，只會呈現已經有效的做法，讓你能繼續保持。\n\n記錄越多，發現就越精準。如果這張卡片沒什麼內容，只是需要更多天的資料，而不是需要改變行為。",
    "The risk percentage the app showed you each day." to "App 每天顯示給你的風險百分比。",
    "The story of this record, in plain words" to "用白話說明這筆紀錄的來龍去脈",
    "The stress index built from your heart data." to "根據你的心臟資料建立的壓力指數。",
    "The suggestions come from your profile — worth tracking to find out. Change anything that doesn't fit as you go." to "這些建議來自你的個人檔案，值得追蹤看看。過程中可隨時修改不合適的項目。",
    "The symptoms that tend to follow each trigger" to "每個誘因之後常出現的症狀",
    "The three things pushing hardest on your bucket today, ordered by how much each is contributing to your risk score. Could be triggers you've logged (caffeine, poor sleep, stress) or prodromes you're currently in (yawning, mood shifts, neck stiffness).\n\nEach row shows the item's name, its severity tag (HIGH / MILD / LOW), and a bar showing how much it's adding compared to a fully-overflowing bucket. The more recent and the more severe, the bigger the contribution.\n\nTap the card to open the Risk detail screen and see every contributor in order, not just the top 3." to "今天對你的水桶壓力最大的三項，依各自對風險分數的貢獻程度排序。可能是你記錄過的誘因（咖啡因、睡眠不佳、壓力），也可能是你目前正處於的前驅症狀（打哈欠、情緒變化、頸部僵硬）。\n\n每一列會顯示項目名稱、嚴重程度標籤（高 / 輕微 / 低），以及一條長條，表示它相較於完全滿溢的水桶所增加的程度。越近期、越嚴重，貢獻就越大。\n\n點選卡片可開啟風險詳情畫面，依序查看所有影響因素，而不只是前 3 項。",
    "The wall part opens the chest and gives you something honest to measure against. If your elbows and wrists cannot stay near it, that is the tightness. The bed part trains the small front muscles: lifting your head a finger's width with the chin tucked works them without letting the big ones cheat. Of everything in these routines, that lift has the best trial results behind it." to "靠牆的部分能打開胸口，也給你一個誠實的衡量標準。如果你的手肘和手腕無法貼近牆面，就表示那裡緊繃。床上的部分訓練前側的小肌肉：下巴內收、把頭抬起一指寬的高度，可以練到這些肌肉，又不讓大肌肉偷力。在這些練習中，這個抬頭動作有最好的試驗結果支持。",
    "The written summary of how treatment has gone." to "治療經過的書面摘要。",
    "Their own site" to "自己的網站",
    "Their posts and replies are now hidden for you. We have been notified." to "他們的貼文和回覆現在已對你隱藏，我們也已收到通知。",
    "Then" to "接著",
    "TheraSpecs" to "TheraSpecs",
    "Therapy" to "治療",
    "ThermaZone" to "ThermaZone",
    "These AI curators will flag relevant articles for your migraine profile and add them to your feed automatically. We've pre-selected the ones that best match your profile." to "這些 AI 策展員會為你的偏頭痛個人檔案挑出相關文章，並自動加入你的動態。我們已先選好最符合你個人檔案的項目。",
    "These answers are the starting point. What the app actually does each day comes from Manage Items and Risk Model, and the weekly check-in nudges those as it learns from what you log. Editing a section here re-runs the setup for that page and asks the AI to re-check your profile straight away." to "這些答案是起點。App 每天實際的運作來自「管理項目」和「風險模型」，每週檢視會根據你的記錄調整這些內容。在這裡編輯某個區段，會重新執行該頁的設定，並請 AI 立即重新檢查你的檔案。",
    "These are being rewritten in your language and were not ready when this report was made. Generate the report again in a few minutes to include them." to "這些內容正在以你的語言重新撰寫，產生這份報告時尚未完成。請過幾分鐘後重新產生報告，即可包含這些內容。",
    "These are estimates. Tap a food to change it, untick anything we got wrong, and correct the portions before adding." to "這些是估計值。點選食物可更換，取消勾選我們判斷錯誤的項目，並在新增前修正份量。",
    "These are the two stretches a physiotherapist gives for exactly that. The hand is there to add a little weight, never to pull. Held long enough, the muscle lets go rather than fighting back." to "這是物理治療師針對這種情況會教的兩個伸展動作。手只是用來增加一點重量，絕不是用力拉。維持夠久，肌肉就會放鬆，而不是對抗。",
    "These migraines: %s." to "這些偏頭痛：%s。",
    "These triggers are checked daily at 9 AM your local time." to "這些誘因會在你當地時間每天上午 9 點檢查。",
    "These triggers are checked every hour as new data arrives." to "這些誘因會在有新資料時每小時檢查一次。",
    "These were added automatically. Tap Undo to remove anything that's not right." to "這些是自動加入的。若有不對的項目，點選「復原」即可移除。",
    "They were usually over in %s" to "通常在 %s 內結束",
    "They will not be able to see any of your diary from now on. Anything they already wrote down stays with them." to "從現在起，他們將無法看到你的任何日記。他們已經記下的內容會保留在他們那裡。",
    "Thiamin" to "硫胺素",
    "Thiamin (B1)" to "硫胺素(B1)",
    "Thiamin high" to "硫胺素偏高",
    "Thiamin low" to "硫胺素偏低",
    "Thirst" to "口渴",
    "This Cliniko login is not set up as a practitioner, so it cannot take appointments." to "這個 Cliniko 登入帳號尚未設定為執業者,因此無法接受預約。",
    "This Week" to "本週",
    "This action can't be undone." to "此動作無法復原。",
    "This allows the app to run background tasks without being killed by Android.\n\n" to "這樣應用程式就能在背景執行工作,不會被 Android 終止。\n\n",
    "This attack will not be imported." to "這筆發作不會被匯入。",
    "This can't be undone." to "此操作無法復原。",
    "This feature requires a premium subscription." to "此功能需要 Premium 訂閱。",
    "This file was already imported." to "這個檔案已經匯入過了。",
    "This goal is no longer on your plan." to "這個目標已不在你的計畫中。",
    "This is information, not medical advice or a diagnosis, and nothing here is a reason to change or stop a medicine on your own. It is here so you can raise it with your doctor." to "這只是資訊,並非醫療建議或診斷,這裡的內容也不構成你自行更改或停用藥物的理由。提供這些內容,是方便你與醫師討論。",
    "This is optional — you can skip straight to logging manually" to "這是選填的,你可以直接跳過,改為手動記錄",
    "This is your full trigger pool: every trigger that can be picked in the wizard, Quick Log, or Daily Check-In, plus every trigger that gets auto-fired from your wearable, weather, nutrition or menstruation data.\n\nFor each trigger:\n• Tap the star to pin it as a favourite. Favourites show up first in Quick Log and in the wizard, so put your most-logged ones up top.\n• Tap the row to expand it. From there you can change the category, set the severity (HIGH / MILD / LOW / NONE — NONE keeps it in the pool but stops it contributing to your risk score), and for auto-detected triggers, toggle the automation on/off and set the threshold the app uses to fire it.\n• Tap the trash icon to remove a trigger entirely. Past logged entries aren't affected; the trigger just stops appearing as an option going forward.\n\nUse the + button to add a custom trigger your doctor mentioned or that you've noticed isn't in the defaults. Manual triggers don't auto-fire, you log them yourself.\n\nChanges to severity, category, automation and thresholds save together when you tap Save & Recalculate at the bottom. That recomputes your risk score so the gauge reflects the new weights immediately." to "這是你完整的誘因清單:包含在精靈、快速記錄或每日檢視中可以選擇的所有誘因,以及根據你的穿戴裝置、天氣、營養或月經資料自動觸發的所有誘因。\n\n每個誘因都可以這樣操作:\n• 點星號可將它設為常用。常用項目會優先顯示在快速記錄和精靈中,所以請把你最常記錄的放在最上面。\n• 點該列可展開。你可以在這裡變更類別、設定嚴重程度(高 / 輕微 / 低 / 無——「無」會讓它留在清單中,但不再計入你的風險分數);若是自動偵測的誘因,還可以開關自動化,並設定應用程式觸發它的門檻。\n• 點垃圾桶圖示可完全移除某個誘因。過去已記錄的內容不受影響,只是之後不會再出現在選項中。\n\n如果你的醫師提到某個誘因,或你發現預設清單裡沒有,可以用 + 按鈕新增自訂誘因。手動誘因不會自動觸發,需要由你自己記錄。\n\n嚴重程度、類別、自動化和門檻的變更,會在你點選底部的「儲存並重新計算」時一併儲存。這會重新計算你的風險分數,讓儀表立即反映新的權重。",
    "This lets Android share app usage totals with MigraineMe. " to "這樣 Android 就能與 MigraineMe 分享應用程式的使用時間總計。",
    "This may take up to 30 seconds" to "最多可能需要 30 秒",
